<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;some&nbsp;general&nbsp;stuff</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This was cute, really. It had a little bit of that warm, fuzzy feeling by the end. Though, I was a little bummed out that this felt quite a bit more&#8230; underwhelming than I expected? Idk, to me it feels&#8230; like the conflict ended&#8230; too early and hence felt a little rushed?<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-81573-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-81573-1')">1</a></sup> From Star Journal-2 to -3, it felt like, there was kind of a gap in between that I was left out in the dark? I mean, it's understandable that they would provide the relevant amenities to 5827 when she was like, superheating the room and seemingly hurting her, but it felt&#8230; a little weird when it ended a little too early? So, it felt like, there was a bit of a weird blip in pacing, as we sense a little bit of that sadness that 5827 is feeling but then she suddenly sounds a lot better without a bit more of something in between? Idk.</p>
<p>I think this bit was the one sorta, holding me back a little bit from upvoting. Novote.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;some&nbsp;very&nbsp;nitpicky&nbsp;stuff</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5827’s secondary property is to move and create stars outside of our solar system.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;is to&quot; sounds a tad weird here in this sentence; maybe &quot;&#8230;property is the ability to move&#8230;&quot;? Idk if &quot;ability&quot; and &quot;property&quot; are the same thing, so, uh, it's up to you.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>SCP-5827:</strong> Um… Can I talk to you about something, Dr. Kara? Sometimes, my head starts to hurt and I feel like… I need to move the stars.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Idk but, the transition from the previous line to this line felt&#8230; a little off? Maybe something like a &quot;<em>(A pause.)</em>&quot; or something to give a bit of that breathing space? Her going from enthusiastic about learning science and then complaining about her pain sounded a little weird imo. And the foreword did say that Dr. Kara entered a conversation <em>after</em> 5827 began to like, say she had pains in her body, so it kinda felt&#8230; weird that 5827 starts off with books and only mentions the issue later on? Idk.</p>
</div>
</div>
