<p>Alright, over all, good crit that I mostly agree with.</p>
<p>The reason for the praise and the journals having nothing else to focus on, is the fact that this child has literally NOTHING going on in her life besides a somewhat nice researcher. If you think about it, if you were to be isolated from society for a few years, then the few people that you've been around have made no attempt to talk to you or do anything for you, then suddenly someone does, you would probably do the same. Even from study from adults being in solitary confinement, there are irreversible effects on the brain. I've worked in a school as a student teacher, and I've watched children cling to their teacher or even me when there is nothing going on at home, or their parents don't give them enough attention.</p>
<p>Actually, I shaped this SCP on a girl I helped teach last semester. She was 7 I think, anyway she fascinated with stars and her parents weren't there. All she would write about was the teacher in charge of the class room and how much she wished the teacher would adopt her. I wrote from how she would talk and how she would act. All the teacher did with her was talk to her, much like how I made Kass act, and this girl became attached to this teacher.</p>
<p>With the picture at the end, I stated in my author post that it was soon to change.</p>
<p>Thank you.</p>

